The '''Battle of Bordeaux''' ({{langx|cs|Bitva u Bordeaux}}, {{langx|pt|Batalha de Bordéus}}, {{langx|fr|Bataille de Bordeaux}}) is an informal name for the  [[1938 FIFA World Cup]] quarter-final tie between [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]] and [[Czechoslovakia national football team|Czechoslovakia]] on 12 June 1938 at [[Parc Lescure]] in [[Bordeaux]], France. The match had a series of brutal fouls by both sides due to the lax officiating of Hungarian referee Pál von Hertzka.

==Match==
===Summary===
[[File:WC 1938 BRA - CSK Bordeaux.jpg|thumb|left|The Czechoslovak players celebrating their goal]]
At the match, which also opened the rebuilt [[Stade du Parc Lescure]], Brazil took the lead 1–0, with Czechoslovakia equalizing on a [[Penalty kick (association football)|penalty kick]] for ball handling by [[Domingos da Guia]]. [[Zezé Procópio]] was sent off after fourteen minutes, while [[Arthur Machado]] and Czechoslovakia's [[Jan Říha]] were sent off just before full time.<ref>Glanville, Brian: "The History of the World Cup", Faber and Faber, London. P. 38</ref> It was the first time that three players were sent off in a World Cup match, a record that was equalled at the [[Battle of Berne (1954 FIFA World Cup)|Battle of Berne 1954]] between Hungary and Brazil, and exceeded at the [[Battle of Nuremberg (association football)|2006 World Cup match]] between Portugal and Netherlands. Captain [[František Plánička]] and [[Oldřich Nejedlý]] suffered a broken right arm and right leg respectively in the mayhem, while [[Josef Košťálek]] was injured in the stomach. 

The match was drawn 1–1 after 90 minutes of full-time, and a 30-minute extra time had to be played. Nejedlý had been ruled out before the end of regulation time due to his injury, but Plánička stayed at the Czechoslovak goal in pain through the rest of the second half and extra time. Three other Brazilians, including [[Leônidas (footballer, born 1913)|Leônidas]] and [[José Perácio]], also left the pitch with injuries.<ref name="day">{{cite web |url=http://tdifh.blogspot.com/2009/06/12-june-1938-battle-of-bordeaux.html |title=12 June 1938 - The Battle of Bordeaux |access-date=October 13, 2019 |last= |first= |date= 12 June 2009|work=This day in football history |publisher= |location= |language= |quote= |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160922152727/http://tdifh.blogspot.com/2009/06/12-june-1938-battle-of-bordeaux.html |archive-date=September 22, 2016 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="guide">{{cite web |url=http://www.worldcupbrazil.net/world-cup-history/world-cup-30s-60s/1938-france/ |title=1938 - France |access-date=October 13, 2019 |last= |first= |date= |work=World Cup guide |publisher= |location= |language= |quote= |archive-date=13 October 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191013182825/http://www.worldcupbrazil.net/world-cup-history/world-cup-30s-60s/1938-france/ |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.elcincocero.com/noticias/detalle/33-mundial-2014/3254-la-batalla-de-burdeos-brasil-vs-checoslovaquia-en-1938 |title=La 'Batalla de Burdeos': Brasil vs Checoslovaquia en 1938 |access-date=October 14, 2019 |last=Monroy |first=Nicolás |date=July 8, 2018 |work=ElCincoCero |publisher= |location= |language=Spanish |quote= |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221013102444/https://www.elcincocero.com/noticias/detalle/33-mundial-2014/3254-la-batalla-de-burdeos-brasil-vs-checoslovaquia-en-1938 |archive-date=October 13, 2022 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.olympodeportivo.es/la-batalla-de-burdeos-mundial-1938/ |title=Brasil, Checoslovaquia y la Batalla de Burdeos |access-date=October 14, 2019 |last=Bonachera |first=Rocío |date=June 12, 2014 |work=Olympo Deportivo |publisher=Olympo Media |location= |language=Spanish |quote= |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191014190441/http://www.olympodeportivo.es/la-batalla-de-burdeos-mundial-1938/ |archive-date=14 October 2019 |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.infobae.com/2014/03/24/1552383-francia-1938-el-dia-que-brasil-cambio-el-jogo-bonito-la-violencia-extrema/ |title=Francia 1938: el día que Brasil cambió el 'jogo bonito' por la violencia extrema |access-date=October 14, 2019 |last= |first= |date=March 24, 2014 |publisher=[[Infobae]] |location= |language=Spanish |quote= |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191014190339/https://www.infobae.com/2014/03/24/1552383-francia-1938-el-dia-que-brasil-cambio-el-jogo-bonito-la-violencia-extrema/ |archive-date=October 14, 2019 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="playoff">{{cite web |url=https://playoffmagazine.com/la-batalla-de-burdeos/ |title=La Batalla de Burdeos |access-date=October 14, 2019 |last=González |first=Eduardo |date=June 15, 2018 |work=Play-Off Magazine |publisher= |location= |language=Spanish |quote= |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191014190441/https://playoffmagazine.com/la-batalla-de-burdeos/ |archive-date=October 14, 2019 |url-status=live }}</ref>

